    "done_when": "scripts/figures_jt60sa_signals.py is a thin imas-ink caller. One function, _read_pulse_ids(pulse_dir, ids_name), opens pulse_dir / f\"{ids_name}.nc\" with imas.DBEntry(path, \"r\") and get(ids_name, autoconvert=False), where pulse_dir is JT60SA_ROOT / \"ids\" / \"101154\" and JT60SA_ROOT comes from imas_ambix.data.paths. The script passes imas_ink.extract_signal_traces(pf_active, \"coil/current\") plus extract_signal_traces(magnetics, \"ip\") to time_trace_figure_mpl, one panel per series, and writes the figure through imas_ink.io.render_to_bytes(format=\"svg\") to docs/figures/jt60sa-signals/jt60sa-E101154-pf-coil-currents.svg. It prints each series' ylabel and units.\ngrep -cE 'VirtualZarrView|read_channel|signal_map|TimeSeries\\(' scripts/figures_jt60sa_signals.py returns 0. git rm deletes docs/figures/jt60sa-signals/jt60sa-E101154-flux-loops.svg and docs/figures/jt60sa-signals/jt60sa-C060033-pf-coil-currents.svg, so that directory holds exactly one SVG and no PNG.\nThe script runs in place (this host is a compute node, SLURM_JOB_ID set) with EXIT=0, and its log shows ten coil names CS1 to EF6 in A plus ip in A. Rasterise the SVG with `convert -density 60` into the run directory and confirm no legend and exactly one 'Time [s]' label. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-signal-figures-from-ids/jtfig-ids-redraw.html embeds the SVG at /imas-ambix/figures/jt60sa-signals/jt60sa-E101154-pf-coil-currents.svg with a caption naming shot E101154, the IDS paths pf_active/coil/current and magnetics/ip, and the unit A.\nDo not edit any plan or the jtfig-signal-figures fragment; the coordinator repairs those. 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests scripts/figures_jt60sa_signals.py' exits 0.",
